 "result_text": "I changed `partition_asymmetry` in `neurom/features/bifurcation.py` so the Uylings variant returns `0.0` when both children are leaves, instead of raising `NeuroMError`. I didn't run the tests or the function.\n\nYou were right about the problem. A bifurcation whose children are both leaves has `n + m == 2`, which hit the old error check. The Uylings denominator `n + m - 2` is zero there, so any morphology with such a bifurcation (every real one) failed. Returning 0 is reasonable because two single-node children are perfectly symmetric.\n\nI left the node counting alone. Uylings defines `n` and `m` as terminal-tip counts, but the code counts all nodes in each child subtree. I didn't change that because it's beyond what the issue asked for.",
